{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And if the entire assembly of …</b> In Torat Kohanim they expounded: ״עֲדַת״ — this is the Sanhedrin; it says ״עֵדָה״ here and it says ״עֵדָה״ further on (Numbers 35:24–25). ״יִשְׂרָאֵל״ — they expounded: the select among Israel, which is the court of seventy-one. ״יִשְׁגּוּ״ — one might think the select members are liable for an error of action; it is taught: ״וְנֶעְלַם״ — they are not liable except for the concealment of a matter. And they said further: if the court issued a ruling and the people acted — one might think they are liable; it is taught: ״הַקָּהָל וְעָשׂוּ״ — the ruling is by the court and the action is by the assembly. Up to here." "And by way of remez it further intends: if the assembly errs and goes astray from the straight path, the Torah of the Sanhedrin of Israel will also become hidden from them, because they did not attend to the assembly of HaShem to straighten what is crooked — for one sin gives birth to another. Go out and learn (Gittin 60a) from the ruling of Abbaye without receiving permission from his master, who erred in that very ruling, and he perceived that this was its consequence — as is stated in Sanhedrin (5a)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:53:01.658346098Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}